WEBVTT

00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.245
I think he wants us to
pick up what he left off.

00:00:08.081 --> 00:00:10.054
Saving people, hunting things...

00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:11.187
Family business.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.253
I don't understand the blind
faith you have in the man.

00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:16.770
It's called being a good son!

00:00:19.238 --> 00:00:22.339
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:00:30.366 --> 00:00:31.846
If only your boys

00:00:32.497 --> 00:00:34.388
Knew how much their daddy loved them.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:43.792
Dad?

00:00:49.673 --> 00:00:51.919
Did he say anything to you? No.

00:00:54.463 --> 00:00:56.295
I'm dealing with dad's death.

00:00:57.484 --> 00:00:58.455
Are you?

00:02:51.521 --> 00:02:52.900
Listen to her purr.

00:02:52.904 --> 00:02:54.578
You ever heard anything so sweet?

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.398
If you two want to get a
room, just let me know, Dean.

00:02:57.403 --> 00:02:59.126
Oh, don't listen to him, baby.

00:02:59.131 --> 00:03:00.399
He doesn't understand.

00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:03.142
You're in a good mood.

00:03:03.147 --> 00:03:04.336
Why shouldn't I be?

00:03:05.215 --> 00:03:06.181
No reason.

00:03:06.196 --> 00:03:07.409
I got my car,

00:03:07.535 --> 00:03:08.673
I got a case.

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:09.977
Things are looking up.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:15.160
You hear of a couple of severed
heads and a pile of dead cows,

00:03:15.165 --> 00:03:16.876
And you're mr. Sunshine.

00:03:17.673 --> 00:03:19.114
How far to Red Lodge?

00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:21.877
Uh, about another 300 miles.

00:03:22.662 --> 00:03:23.553
Good.

00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:30.880
The murder investigation is ongoing,

00:03:30.897 --> 00:03:33.100
And that's all I can share
with the press at this time.

00:03:33.105 --> 00:03:34.997
Sure, sure, we understand
that. But just for the record,

00:03:35.122 --> 00:03:36.824
You found the first uh...

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.563
Head last week, correct?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.103
Okay, and the other, a...

00:03:41.106 --> 00:03:43.572
Christina Flannigan?
That was two days ago.

00:03:43.575 --> 00:03:44.848
Excuse me, Sir.

00:03:45.926 --> 00:03:46.966
Thank you.

00:03:47.442 --> 00:03:49.134
Sorry, boys, time's up.

00:03:49.139 --> 00:03:50.397
We're done here. One last question.

00:03:50.404 --> 00:03:51.903
What about the cattle? Excuse me?

00:03:51.908 --> 00:03:53.282
You know, the cows found dead,

00:03:53.414 --> 00:03:56.695
Split open, drained...
Over a dozen cases.

00:03:57.714 --> 00:03:58.582
What about them?

00:03:58.587 --> 00:04:00.240
So, you don't think
there's a connection?

00:04:01.598 --> 00:04:04.807
Connection with... First,

00:04:04.821 --> 00:04:07.146
Cattle mutilations, now...

00:04:07.152 --> 00:04:10.089
Now, two murders? Kind of
sounds like ritual stuff.

00:04:10.091 --> 00:04:12.800
You know, like satanic
cult ritual stuff.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.952
You're not kidding. No.

00:04:26.617 --> 00:04:29.192
Those cows aren't being mutilated.

00:04:29.571 --> 00:04:31.625
You want to know how I know? How?

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:34.946
Because there's no such
thing as cattle mutilation.

00:04:34.953 --> 00:04:37.207
Cow drops, leave it in the sun,

00:04:37.211 --> 00:04:40.952
Within 48 hours the bloat
will split it open so clean

00:04:40.955 --> 00:04:42.636
It's just about surgical.

00:04:42.642 --> 00:04:46.715
The bodily fluids fall down
into the ground, get soaked up,

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:49.031
'Cause that's what gravity does.

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:52.245
But, hey, it could be Satan.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.379
What newspaper did
you say you worked for?

00:04:57.399 --> 00:04:59.776
World Weekly News. Weekly World News.

00:04:59.779 --> 00:05:02.627
World... I'm new. Weekly world.

00:05:04.529 --> 00:05:06.995
Get out of my office.

00:05:15.994 --> 00:05:16.955
John.

00:05:16.958 --> 00:05:18.973
Jeff. Jeff, I know that.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.804
Dr. Dorkin needs to see you
in his office right away.

00:05:21.808 --> 00:05:23.599
But dr. Dorkin's on vacation.

00:05:23.604 --> 00:05:26.179
He's back, and he's pissed,
and he's screaming for you, man.

00:05:26.184 --> 00:05:27.678
So, if i were you, I would...

00:05:33.342 --> 00:05:35.710
Hey, those satanists in Florida, they
marked their victims, didn't they?

00:05:35.724 --> 00:05:37.678
Yeah, reverse pentacle on the forehead.

00:05:38.866 --> 00:05:41.975
So much of that crap happens in Florida.

00:05:48.062 --> 00:05:49.523
All right. Open it.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.222
You open it.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:53.641
Wuss.

00:06:03.022 --> 00:06:04.404
Well, no pentagram.

00:06:05.172 --> 00:06:07.184
Poor girl. Maybe we should, uh,

00:06:07.189 --> 00:06:08.611
Look in her mouth, see if

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:12.123
This wacko stuffed anything down her
throat, you know, kind of like the moth in

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:13.689
"Silence of the Lambs".

00:06:14.336 --> 00:06:16.752
Yeah, yeah, go ahead. No, you go ahead.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.350
W hat?

00:06:18.353 --> 00:06:19.843
"Put the lotion in the basket".

00:06:20.724 --> 00:06:22.734
Right, yeah, I'm the wuss, huh?

00:06:23.614 --> 00:06:24.554
Whatever.

00:06:31.454 --> 00:06:32.777
Dean, get me a bucket.

00:06:32.799 --> 00:06:34.645
Find something? No, I'm gonna puke.

00:06:38.805 --> 00:06:40.766
All right, lift her lip up again. What?

00:06:42.069 --> 00:06:44.734
You want me to throw up, is that
it? No, I think I saw something.

00:06:49.499 --> 00:06:50.898
Is that a hole?

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:55.066
It's a tooth. Sam, that's a fang.

00:06:57.931 --> 00:07:00.849
Retractable set of vampire
fangs. You got to be kidding me.

00:07:00.854 --> 00:07:02.734
Well, this changes things.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.012
You think?

00:07:31.282 --> 00:07:32.674
How's it going?

00:07:33.071 --> 00:07:34.179
Living  the dream.

00:07:34.184 --> 00:07:35.927
What can I get for
you? Two beers, please.

00:07:38.152 --> 00:07:39.732
So, we're looking for some people.

00:07:40.862 --> 00:07:42.542
Sure. It's hard to be lonely.

00:07:45.159 --> 00:07:46.468
Yeah, but, um,

00:07:48.019 --> 00:07:49.190
That's not what I meant.

00:07:56.353 --> 00:07:58.215
Great. So, these people

00:07:58.293 --> 00:08:00.002
Would've moved here
about six months ago,

00:08:00.007 --> 00:08:01.861
Probably pretty rowdy, like to drink.

00:08:01.867 --> 00:08:03.538
Yeah, real night owls, you know?

00:08:03.541 --> 00:08:05.464
Sleep all day, party all night.

00:08:05.591 --> 00:08:07.836
Barker farm got leased
out a couple months ago.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.103
Real winners. They've
been in here a lot.

00:08:10.199 --> 00:08:12.271
Drinkers, noisy.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.680
I had to 86 them once or twice.

00:08:18.229 --> 00:08:19.019
Thanks.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:36.096
Smile. What?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.476
Show us those pearly
whites. For the love of...

00:09:38.813 --> 00:09:40.673
You want to stick that
thing some place else?

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:41.851
I'm not a vampire.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:43.777
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:44.001 --> 00:09:45.194
I heard you guys in there.

00:09:45.198 --> 00:09:47.170
What do you know about
vampires? How to kill them.

00:09:47.364 --> 00:09:48.555
Now, seriously, bro,

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.503
That knife's making me itch.

00:09:54.524 --> 00:09:55.673
Easy there, chachi.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:04.169
See?

00:10:05.347 --> 00:10:06.197
Fangless.

00:10:06.524 --> 00:10:07.623
Happy?

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:11.395
Now,

00:10:12.316 --> 00:10:13.374
Who the hell are you?

00:10:14.302 --> 00:10:16.146
Sam and Dean Winchester.

00:10:19.057 --> 00:10:20.072
I can't believe it.

00:10:20.642 --> 00:10:22.050
You know, I met your old man once.

00:10:22.048 --> 00:10:23.471
Hell of a guy, great hunter.

00:10:24.817 --> 00:10:25.846
I heard he passed.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.601
I'm sorry.

00:10:27.887 --> 00:10:29.086
It's big shoes,

00:10:29.234 --> 00:10:31.174
But, from what I hear,
you guys fill them.

00:10:31.293 --> 00:10:33.182
Great trackers, good in a tight spot.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.932
You seem to know a lot about our family.

00:10:34.936 --> 00:10:36.175
Word travels fast.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.645
You know how hunters
talk. No, we don't actully.

00:10:38.792 --> 00:10:40.802
I guess there's a lot your
dad never told you, huh?

00:10:43.188 --> 00:10:44.427
So, um...

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.941
So, those two vampires,
they were yours, huh?

00:10:47.949 --> 00:10:48.876
Yep.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:49.920
Been here two weeks.

00:10:49.925 --> 00:10:51.868
Did you check out that
Barker farm? It's a bust.

00:10:51.873 --> 00:10:53.394
Just a bunch of hippie freaks.

00:10:53.549 --> 00:10:55.722
Though they could kill with
that patchouli smell alone.

00:10:55.727 --> 00:10:56.746
Where's the nest, then?

00:10:59.251 --> 00:11:00.401
I got this one covered.

00:11:01.491 --> 00:11:02.572
Look, don't get me wrong.

00:11:02.576 --> 00:11:04.166
It's a real pleasure meeting you fellas,

00:11:04.232 --> 00:11:06.003
But I've been on this
thing for over a year.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.687
I killed a fang back in Austin,
tracked the nest all the way up here.

00:11:10.156 --> 00:11:10.984
I'll finish it.

00:11:11.911 --> 00:11:13.225
We could help.

00:11:13.269 --> 00:11:14.409
Thanks, but, uh,

00:11:14.736 --> 00:11:16.435
I'm kind of a
go-It-Alone type of guy.

00:11:16.492 --> 00:11:18.282
But man, I've been itching for a hunt.

00:11:18.739 --> 00:11:19.520
Sorry.

00:11:19.524 --> 00:11:22.217
But, hey, I hear there's a
chupacabra two states over.

00:11:22.395 --> 00:11:23.854
Go ahead and knock yourselves out.

00:11:30.187 --> 00:11:31.787
It was real good meeting you, though.

00:11:32.837 --> 00:11:34.610
I'll buy you a drink on the flip side.

00:14:15.092 --> 00:14:16.140
So, uh,

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.352
I guess I got to buy you that drink.

00:14:37.312 --> 00:14:38.090
No, no,

00:14:38.306 --> 00:14:39.154
I got it.

00:14:39.159 --> 00:14:40.569
Come on. I insist.

00:14:41.669 --> 00:14:42.567
Thank you, sweetie.

00:14:46.147 --> 00:14:47.578
Another one bites the dust.

00:14:47.583 --> 00:14:48.311
That's right.

00:14:58.695 --> 00:15:01.663
You gave that big-Ass fang one
hell of a haircut, my friend.

00:15:01.677 --> 00:15:03.250
That was you. That was beautiful,

00:15:03.264 --> 00:15:05.569
Absolutely beautiful. Yep.

00:15:06.519 --> 00:15:08.290
You all right, Sammy? Yeah, fine.

00:15:08.294 --> 00:15:09.595
Lighten up a little, Sammy.

00:15:09.809 --> 00:15:11.592
He's the only one who
gets to call me that.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:12.787
Okay.

00:15:13.025 --> 00:15:14.021
No offense meant.

00:15:14.027 --> 00:15:16.071
Just celebrating a
little. Job well done.

00:15:16.077 --> 00:15:17.518
Right. Well, um,

00:15:18.216 --> 00:15:21.533
Decapitations aren't my
idea of a good time, I guess.

00:15:21.537 --> 00:15:24.043
Oh,  come on, man, it's
not like it was human.

00:15:24.047 --> 00:15:26.139
You got to have a little
more fun in that job.

00:15:26.145 --> 00:15:28.017
See, that's what I've
been trying to tell him.

00:15:28.033 --> 00:15:29.834
You could learn a thing
or two from this guy.

00:15:34.378 --> 00:15:35.529
Yeah,  I bet I could.

00:15:35.884 --> 00:15:36.651
Look,

00:15:36.747 --> 00:15:38.351
I'm not gonna bring you guys down.

00:15:38.353 --> 00:15:39.887
I'm just gonna go back to the motel.

00:15:40.093 --> 00:15:41.333
You sure? Yeah.

00:15:44.718 --> 00:15:45.600
Sammy...

00:15:47.983 --> 00:15:50.518
Remind me to beat that buzzkill
out of you later, all right?

00:15:54.609 --> 00:15:56.090
Something I said? No, no.

00:15:56.094 --> 00:15:57.618
He just gets that way sometimes.

00:15:58.918 --> 00:15:59.954
Tell you what,

00:16:00.744 --> 00:16:02.404
Match quarters for the next round.

00:16:20.482 --> 00:16:21.239
So

00:16:21.716 --> 00:16:22.926
I picked up this crossbow,

00:16:23.372 --> 00:16:24.916
And I hit that ugly sucker.

00:16:25.012 --> 00:16:26.381
The silver-Tipped arrow,

00:16:26.608 --> 00:16:27.537
Right in his heart.

00:16:28.243 --> 00:16:30.007
Sammy's waiting in the car, and

00:16:30.012 --> 00:16:32.214
Me and my dad take the
thing into the woods,

00:16:32.873 --> 00:16:34.294
Burn it to a crisp.

00:16:34.709 --> 00:16:37.847
I'm sitting there, and I'm looking into
the fire, and I'm thinking to myself,

00:16:39.057 --> 00:16:40.599
I'm 16 years old

00:16:41.755 --> 00:16:44.211
Kids my age are worried about pimples,

00:16:44.215 --> 00:16:45.346
Prom dates.

00:16:46.175 --> 00:16:48.238
I'm seeing things that
they'll never even know,

00:16:49.087 --> 00:16:50.427
Never even dream of.

00:16:53.425 --> 00:16:54.885
So right then, I just sort of...

00:16:55.139 --> 00:16:56.470
Embraced the life?

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:58.849
Yeah.

00:16:59.086 --> 00:17:00.056
Yeah.

00:17:01.805 --> 00:17:02.594
Yeah.

00:17:04.266 --> 00:17:05.407
How'd you get started?

00:17:05.413 --> 00:17:08.316
First time I saw a
vampire, I was barely 18.

00:17:08.485 --> 00:17:10.136
Home alone with my sister.

00:17:10.141 --> 00:17:13.237
I hear the window break in her room.

00:17:14.315 --> 00:17:16.228
I grabbed my dad's gun, run in,

00:17:16.235 --> 00:17:17.715
Try to get it off her.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.848
It was too late.

00:17:19.246 --> 00:17:20.796
So I shoot the damn thing,

00:17:21.103 --> 00:17:24.623
Which, of course, is about as useful
as snapping it with a rubber band.

00:17:24.877 --> 00:17:26.229
It rushes me,

00:17:26.233 --> 00:17:30.155
Picks me up, flings me across
the room, knocks me out cold.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.861
When I wake up,

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:34.130
The vampire's gone...

00:17:34.445 --> 00:17:36.499
My sister's gone.

00:17:36.676 --> 00:17:38.016
And then?

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:39.460
Then...

00:17:41.928 --> 00:17:43.849
Try explaining that one to your family.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:46.801
So I left home...

00:17:48.432 --> 00:17:50.968
And then bummed around
looking for information.

00:17:51.646 --> 00:17:53.560
How you track them, how you kill them.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.193
And I found that fang.

00:17:58.181 --> 00:17:59.975
It was my first kill.

00:18:01.965 --> 00:18:03.417
Sorry about your sister.

00:18:04.024 --> 00:18:04.864
Yeah.

00:18:06.513 --> 00:18:07.522
She was beautiful.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.954
I can still see her, you know,

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.508
The way she was.

00:18:17.307 --> 00:18:19.321
But, hey, that was a long time ago.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.057
I mean,

00:18:21.064 --> 00:18:21.923
Your dad...

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.009
It's got to be rough.

00:18:24.486 --> 00:18:25.385
Yeah.

00:18:27.236 --> 00:18:28.497
Yeah, you know,

00:18:28.784 --> 00:18:30.286
He was just one of those guys.

00:18:31.575 --> 00:18:33.064
Took some terrible beatings,

00:18:33.752 --> 00:18:35.012
Just kept coming.

00:18:36.013 --> 00:18:37.432
So you're always saying to yourself,

00:18:38.651 --> 00:18:39.531
He's indestructible.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.175
He'll always be around.
Nothing can kill my dad.

00:18:45.099 --> 00:18:46.207
And just like that...

00:18:48.574 --> 00:18:49.499
He's gone.

00:18:57.307 --> 00:18:59.291
I can't talk about this to Sammy.

00:18:59.766 --> 00:19:01.931
No, I got to keep my game face on.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.710
But, uh...

00:19:05.799 --> 00:19:08.526
Truth is, I'm not handling it very well.

00:19:11.724 --> 00:19:13.396
I feel like I have this...

00:19:13.402 --> 00:19:14.811
Hole inside you?

00:19:15.932 --> 00:19:18.947
And it just gets bigger and
bigger and darker and darker?

00:19:21.805 --> 00:19:22.695
Good.

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:24.370
You can use it.

00:19:24.535 --> 00:19:25.725
Keeps you hungry.

00:19:26.564 --> 00:19:27.504
Trust me,

00:19:27.509 --> 00:19:30.091
There's plenty out there needs
killing, and this will help you do it.

00:19:32.286 --> 00:19:34.090
It's not a crime to need your job.

00:19:42.839 --> 00:19:43.897
Hardrails roadhouse.

00:19:43.953 --> 00:19:45.867
Hey, Ellen. Sam Winchester.

00:19:45.872 --> 00:19:48.065
Sam, it's good to hear from you.

00:19:48.399 --> 00:19:51.519
You boys are okay, aren't you?
Yeah, yeah, everything's fine.

00:19:51.674 --> 00:19:52.875
Got a question.

00:19:52.879 --> 00:19:53.695
Yeah, shoot.

00:19:53.702 --> 00:19:55.994
You  ever run across a
guy named Gordon Walker?

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:57.431
I know Gordon.

00:19:57.435 --> 00:19:59.130
And? He's a real good hunter.

00:19:59.134 --> 00:20:01.821
Why you're asking, sweetie?
We ran into him on a job.

00:20:01.956 --> 00:20:04.780
We're kind of working with
him. Don't do that, Sam.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:06.727
I...

00:20:06.964 --> 00:20:08.706
I thought you said he was a good hunter.

00:20:08.802 --> 00:20:11.027
Yeah, and Hannibal Lecter's
a good psychiatrist.

00:20:11.042 --> 00:20:13.978
He is dangerous to everyone
and everything around him.

00:20:14.154 --> 00:20:16.968
If he's working on a job, you boys
just let him handle it and you move on.

00:20:17.045 --> 00:20:18.283
Ellen... No, Sam,

00:20:18.288 --> 00:20:20.465
You just listen to what
I'm telling you, okay?

00:20:22.697 --> 00:20:23.828
Right, okay.

00:20:24.385 --> 00:20:25.925
You know why I love this life?

00:20:27.305 --> 00:20:29.106
It's all black and white.

00:20:29.404 --> 00:20:30.652
There's no maybe.

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:32.402
You  find the bad thing,

00:20:32.406 --> 00:20:33.133
Kill it.

00:20:33.741 --> 00:20:36.539
Most people spend their
lives in shades of gray.

00:20:37.444 --> 00:20:39.530
Is this right? Is that wrong?

00:20:39.897 --> 00:20:40.905
Not us.

00:20:41.463 --> 00:20:43.694
Not sure Sammy would
agree with you, but, uh...

00:20:43.923 --> 00:20:46.157
Doesn't seem like your
brother's much like us.

00:20:47.465 --> 00:20:48.887
I'm not saying he's wrong.

00:20:49.202 --> 00:20:50.213
Just different.

00:20:50.456 --> 00:20:51.487
You and me,

00:20:51.573 --> 00:20:52.954
We were born to do this.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.700
It's in our blood.

00:22:51.438 --> 00:22:52.317
Wait!

00:22:53.288 --> 00:22:54.688
Step back, Eli.

00:23:02.394 --> 00:23:04.616
My name's Lenore. I'm
not gonna hurt you.

00:23:04.624 --> 00:23:06.325
We just need to talk. Talk?

00:23:06.582 --> 00:23:07.561
Yeah, okay. But

00:23:07.563 --> 00:23:10.763
I might have a tough time paying
attention to much besides Eli's teeth.

00:23:10.778 --> 00:23:14.606
He won't hurt you, either. You have my
word. Your word? Oh, yeah, great, thanks.

00:23:14.611 --> 00:23:17.367
Listen, lady, no offense, but you're
not the first vampire I've met.

00:23:17.373 --> 00:23:18.895
We're not like the others.

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:20.318
We don't kill humans,

00:23:20.325 --> 00:23:22.567
And we don't drink their blood.
We haven't for a long time.

00:23:22.616 --> 00:23:25.038
What is this? Some kinda joke?
Notice you're still alive.

00:23:29.493 --> 00:23:33.373
Okay, uh, correct me if I'm wrong here,
but shouldn't you be starving to death?

00:23:33.385 --> 00:23:34.928
We found other ways.

00:23:34.932 --> 00:23:35.831
Cattle blood.

00:23:36.208 --> 00:23:37.959
You're telling me you're
responsible for all the...

00:23:37.967 --> 00:23:40.369
It's not ideal. In
fact, it's disgusting.

00:23:40.705 --> 00:23:44.173
But it allows us to
get by. Okay. Uh, why?

00:23:44.191 --> 00:23:45.220
Survival.

00:23:45.988 --> 00:23:48.240
No deaths, no missing locals, no

00:23:48.247 --> 00:23:51.352
Reason for people like you to
come looking for people like us.

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:53.704
And we blend in.

00:23:54.322 --> 00:23:56.425
Our kind is practically extinct.

00:23:56.708 --> 00:23:59.828
It turns out we weren't as high
up the food chain as we imagined.

00:23:59.832 --> 00:24:01.957
Why are we explaining
ourselves to this killer?

00:24:01.962 --> 00:24:03.461
Eli. We choke

00:24:03.465 --> 00:24:06.023
On cow's blood so that
none of them suffer.

00:24:06.028 --> 00:24:08.520
Tonight, they murdered
Conrad, and they celebrated.

00:24:08.527 --> 00:24:11.503
Eli, that's enough.
Yeah, Eli, that's enough.

00:24:11.509 --> 00:24:13.520
What's done is done.

00:24:14.098 --> 00:24:17.044
We're leaving this town tonight.
Then, why did you bring me here?

00:24:17.051 --> 00:24:18.892
Why are you even talking to me?

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:20.491
Believe me, I'd rather not.

00:24:20.493 --> 00:24:21.856
But I know your kind.

00:24:21.862 --> 00:24:23.672
Once you have the scent,
you'll keep tracking us.

00:24:23.677 --> 00:24:25.087
It doesn't matter where we go.

00:24:25.657 --> 00:24:27.156
Hunters will find us.

00:24:27.301 --> 00:24:29.035
So you're asking us not to follow you.

00:24:29.039 --> 00:24:31.302
We have a right to live.
We're not hurting anyone.

00:24:31.308 --> 00:24:32.556
Right, so you keep saying.

00:24:32.612 --> 00:24:34.997
But give me one good reason
why I should believe you.

00:24:38.086 --> 00:24:39.214
Fine.

00:24:40.956 --> 00:24:42.646
You know what I'm going to do?

00:24:45.563 --> 00:24:47.827
I'm going to let you go.

00:24:50.776 --> 00:24:52.296
Take him back.

00:24:52.313 --> 00:24:53.702
Not a mark on him.

00:25:23.347 --> 00:25:25.831
This is the best
pattern I can establish.

00:25:26.127 --> 00:25:27.659
It's sketchy, at best.

00:25:27.661 --> 00:25:30.025
Looks like it's all coming
from this side of town,

00:25:30.133 --> 00:25:32.075
Which means the nest would be
around here someplace, right?

00:25:32.078 --> 00:25:33.612
Yep, that's what I'm thinking.

00:25:33.917 --> 00:25:37.336
Problem is, there's
35, 40 farms out there.

00:25:37.543 --> 00:25:39.615
I searched about half
of them already but

00:25:39.618 --> 00:25:40.920
Nothing yet.

00:25:41.064 --> 00:25:42.615
They're covering their tracks real good.

00:25:42.622 --> 00:25:44.665
I guess we'll just have
to search the other half.

00:25:47.690 --> 00:25:49.295
What time is it? Where is Sam?

00:25:50.023 --> 00:25:51.624
Car's parked outside.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.711
Probably went for a walk.

00:25:54.107 --> 00:25:57.144
Seems like the take-A-Walk
type. Yeah, he is, but...

00:26:01.197 --> 00:26:02.163
Where you been?

00:26:02.481 --> 00:26:03.992
Can I talk to you alone?

00:26:05.231 --> 00:26:06.734
You mind chilling out
for a couple of minutes?

00:26:12.901 --> 00:26:14.784
Dean, maybe we got to rethink this hunt.

00:26:14.789 --> 00:26:15.899
What are you talking about?

00:26:15.905 --> 00:26:16.892
Where were you?

00:26:18.556 --> 00:26:19.654
In the nest.

00:26:19.821 --> 00:26:20.820
You found it?

00:26:20.905 --> 00:26:22.477
They found me, man.

00:26:23.122 --> 00:26:24.856
How did you get out?
How many did you kill?

00:26:26.105 --> 00:26:27.025
None.

00:26:27.442 --> 00:26:30.448
Sam, they didn't just let you
go. That's exactly what they did.

00:26:30.534 --> 00:26:31.922
All right, well, where is it?

00:26:32.529 --> 00:26:33.982
I was blindfolded. I don't know.

00:26:34.198 --> 00:26:35.228
You got to know something.

00:26:35.231 --> 00:26:36.603
We went over that
bridge outside of town,

00:26:36.608 --> 00:26:38.589
But Dean, listen, maybe
we shouldn't go after them.

00:26:38.594 --> 00:26:40.567
Why not? I don't think
they're like other vampires.

00:26:40.655 --> 00:26:41.955
I don't think they're killing people.

00:26:41.957 --> 00:26:42.825
You're joking.

00:26:44.527 --> 00:26:45.970
Then, how do they stay alive

00:26:45.975 --> 00:26:47.637
Or undead or whatever the hell they are?

00:26:47.650 --> 00:26:49.031
The cattle mutilations.

00:26:49.108 --> 00:26:50.948
They said they live off of animal blood.

00:26:51.013 --> 00:26:52.073
And you believed them?

00:26:52.269 --> 00:26:53.268
Look at me, Dean.

00:26:54.608 --> 00:26:56.280
They let me go without a scratch.

00:26:56.837 --> 00:26:57.945
Wait, so you're saying...

00:26:59.588 --> 00:27:01.211
No, man. No way.

00:27:01.274 --> 00:27:03.328
I don't know why they let
you go. I don't really care.

00:27:03.807 --> 00:27:04.863
We find them, and we waste them.

00:27:05.612 --> 00:27:06.653
Why?

00:27:08.394 --> 00:27:10.706
What part of vampires
don't you understand, Sam?

00:27:10.713 --> 00:27:13.076
If it's supernatural, we kill
it. End of story. That's our job.

00:27:13.081 --> 00:27:16.099
No, Dean, that is not our
job. Our job is hunting evil.

00:27:16.256 --> 00:27:18.641
And if these things aren't
killing people, they're not evil.

00:27:18.655 --> 00:27:20.377
Of course, they're killing
people. That's what they do.

00:27:20.382 --> 00:27:21.841
They're all the same, Sam.

00:27:21.886 --> 00:27:23.368
They're not human, okay?

00:27:23.373 --> 00:27:24.935
We have to exterminate
every last one of them.

00:27:24.941 --> 00:27:27.755
No, Dean, I don't think so,
all right? Not this time.

00:27:27.759 --> 00:27:30.165
Gordon's been on those
vamps for a year. He knows.

00:27:30.171 --> 00:27:32.466
Gordon? You're taking his word for it?

00:27:32.470 --> 00:27:34.594
That's right. Ellen says he's bad news.

00:27:34.759 --> 00:27:36.098
You called Ellen?

00:27:36.587 --> 00:27:38.879
And I'm supposed to listen to
her? We barely know her, Sam.

00:27:38.884 --> 00:27:40.465
No thanks. I'll go with Gordon.

00:27:40.471 --> 00:27:42.968
Right, 'cause Gordon's
such an old friend.

00:27:43.944 --> 00:27:45.357
You don't think I can see what this is?

00:27:45.361 --> 00:27:47.265
What are you talking about?
He's a substitute for dad.

00:27:47.478 --> 00:27:49.233
A poor one. Shut up, Sam.

00:27:49.237 --> 00:27:51.963
He's not even close,
Dean, not on his best day.

00:27:51.969 --> 00:27:54.303
You know what, I'm not even...
You slap on this fake smile,

00:27:54.305 --> 00:27:57.384
But I can see right through it
'cause I know how you feel, Dean.

00:27:57.389 --> 00:27:58.386
Dad's dead.

00:27:58.401 --> 00:28:01.219
And he left a hole, and it
hurts so bad you can't take it.

00:28:01.226 --> 00:28:03.801
But you can't just fill up that
hole with whoever you want to.

00:28:04.546 --> 00:28:06.269
It's an insult to his memory.

00:28:08.523 --> 00:28:09.281
Okay.

00:28:20.962 --> 00:28:22.253
You can hit me all you want.

00:28:22.390 --> 00:28:23.417
It won't change anything.

00:28:23.915 --> 00:28:25.145
I'm going to that nest.

00:28:25.250 --> 00:28:26.699
You don't want to tell me where it is?

00:28:26.706 --> 00:28:27.495
Fine.

00:28:27.809 --> 00:28:28.931
I'll find it myself.

00:28:33.230 --> 00:28:33.969
Dean.

00:28:38.099 --> 00:28:38.891
Gordon?

00:28:41.805 --> 00:28:43.055
You think he went after them?

00:28:43.171 --> 00:28:43.900
Probably.

00:28:43.903 --> 00:28:45.606
Dean, we have to stop him. Really?

00:28:45.611 --> 00:28:47.231
'Cause I say we lend a hand.

00:28:47.239 --> 00:28:49.302
Just give me the benefit
of the doubt, would you?!

00:28:49.307 --> 00:28:50.424
You owe me that.

00:28:50.431 --> 00:28:51.501
Yeah, we'll see.

00:28:51.846 --> 00:28:53.157
I'll drive. Give me the keys.

00:28:56.965 --> 00:28:58.308
He snaked the keys.

00:28:59.055 --> 00:29:00.223
I can't believe this.

00:29:01.465 --> 00:29:03.037
I just fixed her up, too.

00:29:08.150 --> 00:29:10.305
So, the bridge, is that all you got?

00:29:10.349 --> 00:29:12.744
The bridge was 4 and 1/2
minutes from their farm.

00:29:12.809 --> 00:29:13.738
How do you know?

00:29:15.078 --> 00:29:15.938
I counted.

00:29:18.441 --> 00:29:22.082
Took a left out of the farm, then
turned right onto a dirt road,

00:29:22.578 --> 00:29:24.692
Followed that for two
minutes slightly uphill

00:29:24.696 --> 00:29:27.123
Then took another quick
right, and we hit the bridge.

00:29:27.436 --> 00:29:28.739
You're good.

00:29:29.867 --> 00:29:31.701
You're a monster pain in the ass...

00:29:32.938 --> 00:29:34.090
But you're good.

00:29:47.448 --> 00:29:50.064
In the truck, thank you.
We can't leave like this.

00:29:50.240 --> 00:29:51.219
Lenore,

00:29:52.027 --> 00:29:53.950
Listen to me. We need to stay and fight.

00:29:53.953 --> 00:29:56.249
They were my friends,
too, Eli, my family.

00:29:56.251 --> 00:29:57.946
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:29:58.339 --> 00:30:00.533
This is self-Defense.
Kill or be killed.

00:30:00.538 --> 00:30:02.502
They can't hunt us if they're dead.

00:30:02.689 --> 00:30:05.222
Killing those three
wouldn't solve anything.

00:30:05.730 --> 00:30:08.717
There's more where they
came from. We're outnumbered.

00:30:09.133 --> 00:30:10.231
This...

00:30:10.389 --> 00:30:12.281
This is all we can do.

00:30:12.827 --> 00:30:15.503
Try and reason... You can't
reason with these people.

00:30:16.180 --> 00:30:18.036
They're gonna kill us all anyway.

00:30:19.252 --> 00:30:21.439
We should at least take
a few of them with us.

00:30:24.908 --> 00:30:26.536
I'm not giving up hope.

00:30:28.312 --> 00:30:29.760
If we can change,

00:30:30.559 --> 00:30:31.929
They can change.

00:30:32.076 --> 00:30:35.203
Now, go into town and gather the others.

00:30:35.206 --> 00:30:36.969
We leave before sunrise.

00:32:04.282 --> 00:32:05.893
Dead man's blood, bitch.

00:32:45.867 --> 00:32:49.287
Sam, Dean, come on in.
Gordon, what's going on?

00:32:49.290 --> 00:32:52.019
Just poisoning Lenore here
with some dead man's blood.

00:32:52.021 --> 00:32:54.549
She's gonna tell us where all her
little friends are, aren't you?

00:32:54.793 --> 00:32:55.573
Want to help?

00:32:55.636 --> 00:32:57.408
Look, man... Grab a knife.

00:32:58.169 --> 00:33:00.409
I was just about to
start in on the fingers.

00:33:07.545 --> 00:33:08.485
Let's all just

00:33:08.619 --> 00:33:09.758
Chill out, huh?

00:33:10.538 --> 00:33:13.200
I'm completely chill.
Gordon, put the knife down.

00:33:13.468 --> 00:33:15.502
It sounds like it's
Sam here needs to chill.

00:33:15.668 --> 00:33:17.718
Just step away from her, all right?

00:33:23.276 --> 00:33:24.286
You're right.

00:33:25.956 --> 00:33:27.347
I'm wasting my time here.

00:33:28.175 --> 00:33:29.727
This bitch will never talk.

00:33:31.238 --> 00:33:33.282
Might as well put her out of her misery.

00:33:34.009 --> 00:33:36.525
I just sharpened it, so
it's completely humane.

00:33:37.072 --> 00:33:40.057
Gordon, I'm letting her go.
You're not doing a damn thing.

00:33:42.997 --> 00:33:45.621
Gordon, let's talk about this.
What's there to talk about?

00:33:45.626 --> 00:33:46.986
It's like I said, Dean.

00:33:46.991 --> 00:33:49.166
No shades of gray. Yeah,

00:33:49.170 --> 00:33:50.421
I hear you.

00:33:50.816 --> 00:33:52.859
And I know how you feel. Do you?

00:33:52.865 --> 00:33:56.122
The vampire that killed your
sister deserved to die, but this...

00:33:57.654 --> 00:33:59.044
Killed my sister.

00:33:59.803 --> 00:34:03.183
That filthy fang didn't kill
my sister. It turned her,

00:34:03.820 --> 00:34:05.229
Made her one of them.

00:34:05.776 --> 00:34:08.862
So I hunted her down
and I killed her myself.

00:34:10.226 --> 00:34:11.343
You did what?

00:34:11.347 --> 00:34:13.653
It wasn't my sister
anymore. It wasn't human.

00:34:14.400 --> 00:34:15.670
I didn't blink.

00:34:16.347 --> 00:34:19.146
And neither would you. So
you knew all along, then.

00:34:19.151 --> 00:34:21.874
You knew the vampires
weren't killing anyone.

00:34:22.092 --> 00:34:23.691
You knew about the cattle,

00:34:23.696 --> 00:34:26.133
And you just didn't
care. Care about what?

00:34:26.238 --> 00:34:28.905
A nest of vampires suddenly acting nice,

00:34:28.909 --> 00:34:31.594
Taking a little time out
from sucking innocent people,

00:34:31.601 --> 00:34:33.142
And we're supposed to buy that?

00:34:33.266 --> 00:34:34.185
Trust me.

00:34:35.766 --> 00:34:37.379
It doesn't change what they are.

00:34:39.218 --> 00:34:40.479
And I can prove it.

00:34:44.771 --> 00:34:45.681
Let him go.

00:34:48.497 --> 00:34:49.354
Now!

00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:52.628
Relax. If I wanted to kill
him, he'd be on the floor.

00:34:53.496 --> 00:34:54.847
Just making a little point.

00:35:10.785 --> 00:35:12.277
Think she's so different?

00:35:14.840 --> 00:35:16.756
Still want to save her? Look at her.

00:35:21.087 --> 00:35:22.317
They're all the same.

00:35:22.986 --> 00:35:23.871
Evil,

00:35:23.968 --> 00:35:25.248
Bloodthirsty.

00:35:31.004 --> 00:35:31.964
No.

00:35:32.554 --> 00:35:33.519
No.

00:35:35.804 --> 00:35:37.488
You hear her, Gordon?

00:35:37.982 --> 00:35:39.001
No.

00:35:46.286 --> 00:35:47.697
We're done here.

00:35:49.298 --> 00:35:51.293
Sam, get her out of here. Yeah.

00:35:58.134 --> 00:35:59.012
Gordon,

00:36:00.825 --> 00:36:02.990
I think you and I got
some things to talk about.

00:36:16.950 --> 00:36:18.048
Get out of my way.

00:36:19.167 --> 00:36:19.945
Sorry.

00:36:20.053 --> 00:36:21.181
You're not serious.

00:36:24.550 --> 00:36:27.084
I'm having a hard time believing
it, too, but I know what I saw.

00:36:27.090 --> 00:36:29.144
If you want those vampires,
you got to go through me.

00:36:37.572 --> 00:36:38.379
Fine.

00:36:59.597 --> 00:37:02.456
What are you doing, man?
You doing this for a fang?

00:37:03.444 --> 00:37:05.677
Come on, Dean, we're
on the same side here.

00:37:05.682 --> 00:37:07.627
I don't think so, you sadistic bastard.

00:37:13.113 --> 00:37:14.843
You're not like your brother.

00:37:14.941 --> 00:37:15.980
You're a killer

00:37:16.226 --> 00:37:17.165
Like me.

00:37:42.943 --> 00:37:44.242
Oh, sorry.

00:37:46.999 --> 00:37:48.045
You know,

00:37:48.956 --> 00:37:50.376
I might be like you.

00:37:51.436 --> 00:37:52.553
I might not.

00:37:58.805 --> 00:38:00.806
But you're the one tied up right now.

00:38:42.089 --> 00:38:43.217
I miss anything?

00:38:44.487 --> 00:38:45.275
Eh, not much.

00:38:47.096 --> 00:38:48.318
Lenore get out okay?

00:38:48.584 --> 00:38:49.282
Yeah,

00:38:49.787 --> 00:38:51.079
All of them did.

00:38:54.527 --> 00:38:56.238
Then, I guess our work here is done.

00:38:59.136 --> 00:39:00.144
How are you doing, Gordie?

00:39:01.543 --> 00:39:02.582
Got to tinkle yet?

00:39:03.451 --> 00:39:04.312
All right.

00:39:05.500 --> 00:39:06.739
Well, get comfy.

00:39:07.356 --> 00:39:10.885
We'll call someone in two or
three days, have them come out

00:39:10.894 --> 00:39:11.913
And untie you.

00:39:13.935 --> 00:39:15.273
Ready to go, Dean?

00:39:16.877 --> 00:39:17.783
Not yet.

00:39:24.387 --> 00:39:25.937
I guess this is goodbye.

00:39:27.447 --> 00:39:28.487
Well, it's...

00:39:28.945 --> 00:39:29.953
It's been real.

00:39:40.971 --> 00:39:41.989
Okay.

00:39:42.496 --> 00:39:43.506
I'm good now.

00:39:44.826 --> 00:39:45.645
We can go.

00:39:59.796 --> 00:40:01.609
Sam. Yeah?

00:40:02.668 --> 00:40:03.558
Clock me one.

00:40:05.147 --> 00:40:06.247
What? Come on.

00:40:06.362 --> 00:40:07.573
I won't even hit you back.

00:40:07.709 --> 00:40:08.525
Let's go.

00:40:10.869 --> 00:40:11.589
No.

00:40:12.246 --> 00:40:14.500
Let's go. You get a
freebie. Hit me. Come on.

00:40:15.198 --> 00:40:17.902
You look like you just went 12
rounds with a block of cement, Dean.

00:40:19.003 --> 00:40:20.104
I'll take a rain check.

00:40:23.932 --> 00:40:25.392
I wish we never took this job.

00:40:25.407 --> 00:40:26.538
It just jacked everything up.

00:40:28.482 --> 00:40:29.308
What do you mean?

00:40:32.839 --> 00:40:35.524
Think about all the hunts we
went on, Sammy, our whole lives.

00:40:36.312 --> 00:40:38.226
What if we killed things
that didn't deserve killing?

00:40:38.761 --> 00:40:40.825
You know? I mean, the way dad raised us.

00:40:41.093 --> 00:40:42.863
Dean, after what happened to mom...

00:40:44.704 --> 00:40:47.481
Dad did the best he
could. I know he did.

00:40:48.982 --> 00:40:50.435
But maybe he wasn't perfect.

00:40:51.030 --> 00:40:53.233
And the way he raised us,
to hate those things...

00:40:53.240 --> 00:40:54.368
And, man, I hate them.

00:40:54.493 --> 00:40:55.804
I do.

00:40:56.022 --> 00:40:58.294
When I killed that vampire at the
mill, I didn't even think about it.

00:40:58.311 --> 00:40:59.742
Hell, I even enjoyed it.

00:41:02.907 --> 00:41:04.248
You didn't kill Lenore.

00:41:04.887 --> 00:41:06.546
No, but every instinct told me to.

00:41:06.955 --> 00:41:08.676
I was gonna kill her. I
was gonna kill them all.

00:41:08.682 --> 00:41:09.971
Yeah, Dean, but you didn't,

00:41:10.437 --> 00:41:11.777
And that's what matters.

00:41:15.759 --> 00:41:16.970
Yeah.

00:41:20.609 --> 00:41:22.240
'Cause you're a pain in my ass.

00:41:25.389 --> 00:41:27.851
I guess I might have to stick
around to be a pain in the ass, then.

00:41:29.244 --> 00:41:30.040
Thanks.

00:41:33.140 --> 00:41:34.117
Don't mention it.

00:00:03.162 --> 00:00:04.668
